{
 ;; Real games: no wizard mode, no human intervention, run until the game ends.
 ;;
 ;; The difference from shell-config.edn is `:no-exit`, which is absent here.
 ;; With `:no-exit true` the framework skips quit-when-idle, quit-when-looping
 ;; and quit-when-stuck - in the original as well as the port - so a bot that
 ;; deadlocks on a prompt it cannot classify simply sits there.  That flag
 ;; exists for comparison runs, where the harness owns the process lifetime; it
 ;; is the wrong setting for a game that is supposed to reach an outcome.
 :bot "mainbot"
 :ttyrec true
 :interface :shell
 :nh-command "/home/roro/work/projects/super_nethack/run_06.09.26/new_bothack/claude/tools/nethack.sh"
}
